# Never ship node_modules, build output, or data into the image context.
#
# Docker matches ignore patterns with filepath.Match semantics, where `*` does
# NOT cross a directory separator. A bare `*.db` therefore only matches a
# database at the context root -- `server/denyut.db` would still be copied in.
# The `**/` prefix is required to match at any depth.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build output (regenerated by the build step)
server/dist/
**/dist/

# SQLite databases. The remote database is authoritative in production and the
# local file is only a development convenience, so never bake it into an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Uploads (scratch space, never needed at build time)
uploads/
**/uploads/

# Local environment files may hold a real Turso token.
.env
**/.env
!.env.example

# Test scripts and scratch files
server/*.cjs
**/*.cjs
**/*.mjs
server/diag.txt
server/denyut.db.bak

# Source workbooks are large and must never be committed or shipped.
*.xlsx
**/*.xlsx

# VCS and deploy metadata
.git/
.gitignore
fly.toml
render.yaml
DEPLOY.md

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
